{% extends "_layouts/default.njk" %}

{% set pageName = "Duplicate record training" %}
{% set headerOptions = {
  service: {
    text: serviceName
  }
} %}

{% block content %}
  <div class="nhsuk-grid-row">
    <div class="nhsuk-grid-column-two-thirds">

      <!-- Duplicate training demo index -->
      <h1 class="nhsuk-heading-l">Duplicate record training</h1>
      <p class="nhsuk-body">Demo scenarios for reviewing duplicate vaccination records at different set sizes, plus design explorations trying out presentation ideas on top of them.</p>

      <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-m">User testing scenarios</h2>
      <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour">Six sets built from real data examples, chained as their own queue: the start page leads into set 1, the next button steps through sets 1 to 6, then returns here.</p>
      <ul class="nhsuk-list">
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/start">Start page</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Content page introducing the review (placeholder copy), with a CTA into set 1</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/test-1">Set 1 (2 records)</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Sparse school-located upload against a rich API record with a full batch, site and dose-specific coding</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/test-2">Set 2 (3 records)</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Two API echoes of one event carrying the same code under two term renderings, plus an upload with the only batch number and dose number</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/test-3">Set 3 (3 records)</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Dose conflict on one day: two records say first dose, one says second, each backed by its own SNOMED code</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/test-4">Set 4 (2 records)</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">GP pair with different real times on the same day: booster coding at the surgery against a dose-specific second dose</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/test-5">Set 5 (2 records)</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Minimal pair: a first-dose API record against an upload with no dose number at all</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/test-6">Set 6 (4 records)</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">One upload and three API echoes of a 12:42pm appointment, coded three ways: second dose, generic booster, pre-school booster</p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-m">Design scenarios</h2>
      <ul class="nhsuk-list">
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/2-records">2 records</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Near-identical pair: the same GP event arriving twice from the NHS Immunisations API</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/3-records">3 records</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Two API echoes plus a sparse historical upload with a divergent date</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/5-records">5 records</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Mixed API and historical upload set wrapping onto a second row, including a long name that wraps within its card</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/3-records-selected">3 records, selection made</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Pre-selected state: preferred record already chosen, tags and highlighted border from load</p>
        </li>
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/20-records">20 records</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Full-scale set: one record made in Mavis among API echoes and historical uploads, with outliers, blank fields and wrapping values</p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      

      <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-m">From a child record</h2>
      <ul class="nhsuk-list">
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/gareth-record">Gareth Greene's MMR record</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">The other way in: a child's MMR vaccination record (as designed on the vaccination-record-valid-ignored-doses branch) whose dose 1 carries a +2 duplicates link. Following it opens the 3-record choosing view without the Review heading, section navigation or queue framing. Record 1's View this record link opens a static copy of the vaccination record view</p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-m">Design explorations</h2>
      <ul class="nhsuk-list">
        <li class="nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-4">
          <a class="nhsuk-link" href="/duplicate-training/3-records-compact">3 records, compact</a>
          <p class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">Optimised for sets of 3 or fewer (4 or more are about 0.5% of duplicates): the same 3-record queue scenario at the standard 1100px page width instead of the 1720px canvas, with three record columns, a narrower label column and tighter gaps and cell padding. Keeps the grey summary card and recessed grid plane of the wide pages</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <!-- /Duplicate training demo index -->

    </div>
  </div>
{% endblock %}
